      "text": "the Lord gives keys of gift, which shall bring to light this ministry, D&C 6:28. keys of ministry given to Peter, James, and John, D&C 7:7 (27:12). Twelve who were with Christ in ministry at Jerusalem will judge Israel, D&C 29:12. bishop or high priests set apart for ministry should be tried only before First Presidency, D&C 68:22. twenty-four elders who had been faithful in work of ministry, D&C 77:5 (Rev. 4:4). commandment to those called to ministry, D&C 84:86. labor diligently, that you may be perfected in your ministry, D&C 88:84 (90:8; 97:13). school of prophets established for those who are called to ministry, D&C 88:127. house to be built for work of ministry of Presidency, D&C 94:3. house to be built for instruction of those called to work of ministry, D&C 97:13–14. descendant of Aaron1 has legal right to keys of ministry of bishop, D&C 107:76. the Lord has given Joseph Smith keys of kingdom and ministry, D&C 115:19. offices given for work of ministry, D&C 124:143. the Lord spent three years in ministry among Jews, D&C 138:25. the Savior’s ministry among dead limited to time between Crucifixion and Resurrection, D&C 138:27.",
